.TH IMMUTABLE 1 "2026-07-23" "immutable 0.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
immutable \- overlay management for immutable Pop!_OS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B immutable
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B immutable
manages BTRFS overlays on an immutable Pop!_OS installation.
Overlays are writable snapshots of the read-only base system
.RB ( @base ),
allowing isolated testing of different package versions without
modifying the base system.
.PP
The
.B immutable
CLI communicates with the
.BR immutable-daemon (8)
over a Unix socket
.RI ( /run/immutable/daemon.sock ).
Users in the
.B immutable
group can manage overlays without root privileges.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI create " name" [" --from " source]
Create a new overlay by snapshotting the current boot overlay.
If
.BI --from " source"
is specified, snapshot from
.I source
instead.
.I source
can be an overlay name,
.BR @base ,
or
.BR @overlay- name.
.TP
.BI shell " name"
Open an interactive shell inside the specified overlay.
The overlay is mounted with chroot, and the user's session
environment
.RI ( WAYLAND_DISPLAY ,
.BR XDG_RUNTIME_DIR ,
etc.)
is forwarded.
.TP
.BI run " name command" "..."
Run a non-interactive command inside the overlay.
Output streams to the terminal in real time.
.TP
.B list
List all overlays with sizes and paths, plus boot configuration.
.TP
.B list-names
List overlay names, one per line.
Designed for scripting and shell completions.
.TP
.BI switch " name"
Update the boot entry to use the specified overlay.
A reboot is required to activate.
.TP
.BI reset " name"
Delete the overlay and re-snapshot it from the current boot
overlay.
Useful for starting fresh without creating a new overlay.
.TP
.BI delete " name"
Delete an overlay.
Cannot delete the currently active boot overlay.
.TP
.B status
Show system status including boot configuration and subvolume
list.
.TP
.B lock
Make
.B @base
read-only.
Prevents accidental modification of the base system.
.TP
.B unlock
Make
.B @base
writable.
Required for running
.B apt
or
.B dpkg
on the base system.
.TP
.B recovery
Switch to the recovery overlay.
.TP
.B reset-recovery
Re-snapshot the recovery overlay from
.BR @base .
.TP
.B clean-boot
Remove stale boot entries from the ESP whose kernel files
no longer exist.
Protected entries
.RI ( immutable.conf ", " recovery.conf ", " previous.conf )
are never removed.
.TP
.BI update-initramfs [" --version " version]
Run
.BR update-initramfs (8)
in the current boot overlay and copy the kernel and initrd
to the ESP.
Only operates on the active boot overlay.
The
.B --version
flag targets a specific kernel version; otherwise the
latest installed kernel is used.
.TP
.B update
Copy the
.B immutable
CLI to
.B /pool/@data/immutable
for persistence across overlays.
.TP
.BR help " |" \-\-help " |" \-h
Show usage information.
.SH OVERLAYS
Overlays are BTRFS subvolumes stored under
.BR /pool/ :
.TP
.B @base
The read-only base system.
Snapshot of the initial installation.
.TP
.B @overlay-\fIname\fR
A writable snapshot of
.B @base
(or another overlay).
Each overlay has its own
.BR /usr ,
.BR /etc ,
and user configuration directories.
.TP
.B @data
Shared user data
.RI ( Documents ", " Downloads ", " Pictures ", etc.).
Bind-mounted into whichever overlay is active.
.TP
.B @overlay-recovery
Fallback overlay used when boot failures are detected.
.SH EXAMPLES
 typical workflow:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
# Create an overlay for testing
$ immutable create cosmic-files-pr123

# Enter the overlay
$ immutable shell cosmic-files-pr123

# Inside: install and test packages
# apt update && apt install cosmic-files

# Exit shell, then switch boot overlay
$ immutable switch cosmic-files-pr123
$ sudo reboot
.fi
.RE
.PP
If the test fails, switch back:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
$ immutable switch init
$ sudo reboot
$ immutable delete cosmic-files-pr123
.fi
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B IMMUTABLE_PASSWORD
If set, used for authentication instead of prompting interactively.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /run/immutable/daemon.sock
Unix socket for daemon communication.
.TP
.B /pool/@base
Read-only base system.
.TP
.B /pool/@data
Shared user data.
.TP
.B /etc/immutable.conf
System configuration (username).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR immutable-daemon (8),
.BR btrfs (8),
.BR systemd-boot (7)
.SH AUTHORS
Pop!_OS immutable base team.
